# Machine-generated literature sweeps: leads, never citable under the rule in
# README.md. Kept on the author's disk.
#
# Removed from all 69 commits with git filter-repo on 16 Nov 2026. This comment
# used to say that happened "before it was made public", which conflated two
# repositories at the same URL -- see STATE.md, "A ref is not the object store".
# THE REPOSITORY THAT EXISTS NOW HAS NEVER BEEN PUBLIC: it is private, has no
# public mirror, and was created on 16 Nov 2026 when its predecessor was deleted
# and recreated under the same name. That PREDECESSOR was public for roughly
# seven minutes, which is the whole reason the deletion was necessary -- orphaned
# research_notes/ objects stayed fetchable by pre-rewrite SHA after the branch
# rewrite, so the host's object store outlived the refs.
#
# In this repository `git log --all -- research_notes/` returns nothing, checked
# 17 Nov 2026. Note what that does and does not establish: it interrogates what
# the refs reach, and that was exactly the insufficient check last time. It is
# adequate here only because this object store was never served publicly.
#
# Do not re-add them. The rule does not depend on who can read the repository
# today -- an unverified lead is read as a finding whatever the label says, and
# this repository is intended for publication.
research_notes/

